From: Marco Casaroli <marco.casaroli@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] compiler-rt/profile: Build __gcov_fork() only with fork()

NuttX declares fork() only with CONFIG_ARCH_HAVE_FORK.  Instrumented code
calls __gcov_fork() only in place of a call to fork(), so nothing needs it
in other configurations.  The second COMPILER_RT_VISIBILITY that follows the
block makes the first one harmless, and the hunks do not touch the line of
the outer #if, which differs between the LLVM versions.

---
 lib/profile/GCDAProfiling.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/lib/profile/GCDAProfiling.c
+++ b/lib/profile/GCDAProfiling.c
@@ -588,2 +588,3 @@
 COMPILER_RT_VISIBILITY
+#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_HAVE_FORK
 pid_t __gcov_fork() {
@@ -602,5 +603,6 @@
   return pid;
 }
 #endif
+#endif
 
 COMPILER_RT_VISIBILITY
